{"id":"c4dd206ee7091798","group":"58","path":"58/batch01/58-df-normal-space.md","title":"Normal Space","display":"df-normal-space — Normal Space","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-normal-space","aliases":["58-df-normal-space","Normal Space","58-df-zfc-top2-normal-space","58-df-zfc-top5-normal-space","58-df-zfc-top6-normal-space"],"display":"df-normal-space — Normal Space","depends_on":["[[../batch12/58-df-topological-space.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-normal-space"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-normal-space</span><span>Normal Space</span><span>58-df-zfc-top2-normal-space</span><span>58-df-zfc-top5-normal-space</span><span>58-df-zfc-top6-normal-space</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-normal-space — Normal Space"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"815e63e5071e7b58\" href=\"?note=815e63e5071e7b58\" title=\"../batch12/58-df-topological-space.md\">../batch12/58-df-topological-space.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X,\\tau\\in V\">\\(X,\\tau\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{TopologicalSpace}_S\">\\(\\operatorname{TopologicalSpace}_S\\)</span> (topological-space predicate; see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"815e63e5071e7b58\" href=\"?note=815e63e5071e7b58\" title=\"../batch12/58-df-topological-space.md\">../batch12/58-df-topological-space.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Normal}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Normal}_S\\)</span> (normal-space predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}normal\\text{-}space} \\vdash \\mathrm{Normal}_S(X,\\tau)\\leftrightarrow \\operatorname{TopologicalSpace}_S(X,\\tau)\\land \\forall A,B\\subseteq X\\;\\left(X\\setminus A\\in\\tau\\land X\\setminus B\\in\\tau\\land A\\cap B=\\varnothing\\to \\exists U,V\\in\\tau\\;(A\\subseteq U\\land B\\subseteq V\\land U\\cap V=\\varnothing)\\right)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}normal\\text{-}space} \\vdash \\mathrm{Normal}_S(X,\\tau)\\leftrightarrow \\operatorname{TopologicalSpace}_S(X,\\tau)\\land \\forall A,B\\subseteq X\\;\\left(X\\setminus A\\in\\tau\\land X\\setminus B\\in\\tau\\land A\\cap B=\\varnothing\\to \\exists U,V\\in\\tau\\;(A\\subseteq U\\land B\\subseteq V\\land U\\cap V=\\varnothing)\\right)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Normal: disjoint closed sets can be separated by disjoint open neighborhoods.</li>\n<li>Metric: every metric space is normal; metrizable <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\implies\">\\(\\implies\\)</span> normal</li>\n<li>Every paracompact Hausdorff space is normal.</li>\n<li>This definition does not build in the <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T_1\">\\(T_1\\)</span> axiom; adding <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T_1\">\\(T_1\\)</span> gives the usual <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T_4\">\\(T_4\\)</span> convention.</li>\n<li>Urysohn's lemma and the Tietze extension theorem are downstream theorems.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Munkres, Topology</li>\n<li>Engelking, General Topology</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch12/58-df-topological-space.md","status":"resolved","id":"815e63e5071e7b58","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch12/58-df-topological-space.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch12/58-df-topological-space.md","status":"resolved","id":"815e63e5071e7b58","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\operatorname{TopologicalSpace}_S$ (topological-space predicate; see [[../batch12/58-df-topological-space.md]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"X,\\tau\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{TopologicalSpace}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Normal}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}normal\\text{-}space} \\vdash \\mathrm{Normal}_S(X,\\tau)\\leftrightarrow \\operatorname{TopologicalSpace}_S(X,\\tau)\\land \\forall A,B\\subseteq X\\;\\left(X\\setminus A\\in\\tau\\land X\\setminus B\\in\\tau\\land A\\cap B=\\varnothing\\to \\exists U,V\\in\\tau\\;(A\\subseteq U\\land B\\subseteq V\\land U\\cap V=\\varnothing)\\right)","display":true},{"tex":"\\implies","display":false},{"tex":"T_1","display":false},{"tex":"T_1","display":false},{"tex":"T_4","display":false}],"bytes":1397,"backlinks":[{"id":"7dc92d5c1637052d","anchor":"ref-1","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-884","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch01/58-df-normal-space.md|58-df-normal-space]]（batch01）"}],"outgoing":["815e63e5071e7b58"]}